{"activity_text": "Antiviral", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Unknown", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Peptide design: WL-1 is a modified version of GF-17 by making the following changes F17W, V21K, F27K, and deleting V32. Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that this sequence shows similarity (76.47%) to GF-17 K: 25%; R: 19%, I=L: 13%. Activity: inhibited herpes simplex virus 1 (HSV-1) infection in epithelial and neuronal cells. Animal model:mouse: beneficial treatment outcomes were observed in HSV-1 ear infected mice after WL-1 treatment.", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "37342565", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Front Microbiol. 2023 Jun 5;14:1201505. doi: 10.3389/fmicb.2023.1201505. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP04774", "source_id": "AP04774", "source_numeric_id": "04774", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP04774", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Cathelicidin-derived antiviral peptide inhibits herpes simplex virus 1 infection.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
